# Trivy Ignore List — Accepted Risks
# Last updated: 2026-05-09
# Review quarterly or when fixed versions become available.

# ecdsa 0.19.1 — Minerva timing attack. No fix available.
# Only used in non-production test utilities. Not exposed to external input.
CVE-2024-23342

# nth-check 1.0.2 — ReDoS in CSS selector parser. Transitive dep of react-scripts.
# Only used at build time (CSS optimization), not at runtime. Low real-world risk.
CVE-2021-3803

# serialize-javascript — RCE via RegExp.flags. Transitive dep of react-scripts/webpack.
# Only used at build time. Not exposed to user input. Blocked by CSP in production.
GHSA-5c6j-r48x-rmvq

# underscore 1.13.6 — DoS via recursive flatten. Transitive dep of react-dev-utils.
# Only used at build time (dev tools). Not exposed to user input.
CVE-2026-27601

# Secret scanning false positives — .env files contain placeholders, not real secrets.
# These are template files committed for documentation purposes.
